==Trivia==
*Soractes' name may be a portmanteau of 空 ''sora'' (sky/the air, correlating with his [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait) and ''[[wikipedia:Socrates|Socrates]]'', an ancient Greek philosopher. While Soractes' Japanese name is written in katakana, the kanji 空 can also be read as ''kara'' or ''kū'', meaning emptiness or the void/aether element in ''[[wikipedia:Godai|godai]]'', a set of five elements in Japanese Buddhist philosophy.
**Soractes' Japanese name is also very similar to ''practice'' (possibly referring to how he is only the first [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] and first major [[Zero Legends]] boss; i.e., [[Adherence to Virtue]] is a practice round compared to what comes next):
***ソラクティス ''Sorakutisu'' (Soractis) → プラクティス ''purakutisu'' (practice)
**Continuing with the topic of philosophy, his pose is seemingly based on the famous 20th century sculpture of [[wikipedia:The Thinker|The Thinker]], or on [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statues_of_Plato_(left)_and_Socrates_(right)_by_Leonidas_Drosis_at_the_Academy_of_Athens.jpg this statue] of Socrates.
**In real life, Socrates was known to have had an upturned nose and bulging eyes, yet Soractes ironically has neither.
**Soractes' seemingly empty head may allude to "I know that I know nothing," a famous saying widely attributed to Socrates.
***This saying is directly referenced by [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]' Korean description, which states that all he knows about cats is that he knows nothing about them.
**Adherence to Virtue may refer to [[wikipedia:Virtue ethics|virtue ethics]], an ethical theory that has its roots in ancient Greece with Socrates, who believed virtue is equivalent to knowledge.
*The capital (top) of Soractes' column appears to combine all three [[wikipedia:Classical orders|orders]] of ancient Greek architecture: [[wikipedia:Doric order|Doric]], [[wikipedia:Ionic order|Ionic]] and [[wikipedia:Corinthian order|Corinthian]].
*According to the Japanese descriptions of Sage of Mind Soractes, [[Sage of Logic Newtone]] and [[Sage of Selection Darvin]], the world they are observing is specifically the [[wikipedia:Present life|present life]] (現世 ''gen sei'', ''utsushi yo''), a concept in certain religions such as Shinto and Buddhism.
*Sage of Mind Soractes can be seen as a foil to [[The Face]]:
**Both are mid-ranged Floating enemies that are predominantly white.
**The Face's diet caused him to lose everything but his face, whereas Soractes has a full body but lacks a face.
**The Face is extremely slow in both movement speed and attack rate, whereas Soractes moves quickly and attacks non-stop.
**Both are bosses of the 48th stages of Japan. The [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]] of [[Empire of Cats]] takes place across the 47 prefectures of Japan and [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]] rather than various countries and the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]], while Adherence to Virtue is the 48th and last Zero Legends stage to take place in a [[Media:Map040.png|jumbled up and mirrored Japan]].
**Adherence to Virtue's [https://youtu.be/_KhgY0ArzW4 theme] contains the leitmotif of "[https://youtu.be/5yyyqU-Y7lA Lunar Battle]", which first plays against The Face.
**Both are the first major bosses of their respective areas (if one does not count [[Metafilibuster (Enemy)|Metafilibuster]] as the first major boss of Zero Legends).

